  "worked_solution": "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $\u0394x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\u0394y={y}_{\\text{new}}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{\u2032}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $\u0394y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394y & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x \\\\  & =({e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+\u0394y$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\u0394y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(1+3{x}_{\\text{new}}) & =y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1+3{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
